# FOLLOWUP_PROPOSAL-2 — OpenCode compilation target for pasture codegen

**Supersedes FOLLOWUP_PROPOSAL-1 (aura-plugins-h78qq, 3/3 reviewer-ACCEPT).** This revision folds in TWO user-mandated Plan-UAT decisions; everything else is unchanged from h78qq.

> **Δ from h78qq (Plan-UAT REVISE):**
> 1. **UAT-D1 — target rename `claude` → `claude-code`.** `HarnessName` const is `HarnessClaudeCode = "claude-code"`; the `-targets` flag DEFAULT is `claude-code`. Output stays **byte-identical** to today — only the target *name* changes, not the emitted bytes. `HarnessOpenCode = "opencode"` unchanged; reserved `HarnessCodex` stays out of the registry.
> 2. **UAT-D2 — generate a minimal committed `opencode.json`.** The `TargetHarness.Manifest` field is now a **real emitter** (not the nil seam). Minimal shape: `$schema` + an explicit `skills.paths` entry pointing at `.opencode/skill`. Agents stay auto-discovered from `.opencode/agent/`.

**Scope (locked):** add an **OpenCode** harness target to pasture's Go codegen pipeline. OpenCode skills + agents + a minimal `opencode.json` + system-wide install. **Codex AND OpenCode hooks (.mjs) are OUT** of this epic — but the abstraction MUST be designed so both slot in later with no rework.

Built on PINNED facts (URD `aura-plugins-udxmb` comments O-2 / O-PERM / O-MODEL / O-GLOBAL; `TargetHarness` naming; the two Plan-UAT decisions UAT-D1/UAT-D2). No re-research; every external fact is source-pinned in the URD.

---

## 1. Problem Space

**Axes**
- **Variation, not multiplication.** One typed protocol source (`specs_data*.go`) must emit N harness dialects. The portable bulk (skill *bodies*) is identical across harnesses; only **frontmatter dialect + output path + agent/manifest packaging** vary. So the design axis is *per-harness routing + dialect selection*, NOT a per-harness fork of the renderers.
- **Has-a / Is-a.** A `TargetHarness` *has-a* skill-path function, *has-a* skill template name, *has-a* agent emitter, *has-a* (now) manifest emitter. Claude-Code/OpenCode/(future Codex) *are-a* `TargetHarness` value in a static compile-time registry. Mirrors the existing `internal/acp/adapter.go` static-registry precedent (no plugin system).
- **Tiers diverge independently.** Tier A = skills (path routing + a frontmatter template; bodies reused verbatim). Tier B = agents (a different frontmatter dialect: `mode`/`model`/`permission`). Tier C = distribution (manifest + file placement, per-repo and system-wide). Each tier is a separable slice.
- **Cost / frequency.** Codegen runs at build time, deterministic, cheap. The expensive failure mode is silent drift (a wrong model id yields a non-functional agent), so model ids and the default-output guarantee get explicit regression tests.

**Why now / why a registry, not config:** exactly two live targets (claude-code, opencode) plus one reserved slot (codex), all known at compile time, all needing Go logic (path math, permission/model mapping, manifest marshalling). A static typed registry is the proportionate complexity. We do **not** build a plugin system, a config-file target loader, or the `.mjs`/Codex emitters (YAGNI — but we leave seams for them, see §8).

---

## 2. The `TargetHarness` abstraction (R1) — concrete Go shape

New file `internal/codegen/harness.go`:

```go
package codegen

import "github.com/dayvidpham/pasture/pkg/protocol"

// HarnessName is the strongly-typed target identifier.
type HarnessName string

const (
	// HarnessClaudeCode is the default Claude Code target (UAT-D1: renamed from
	// the former "claude"). Its emitted bytes are unchanged — only the NAME.
	HarnessClaudeCode HarnessName = "claude-code"
	HarnessOpenCode   HarnessName = "opencode"
	// HarnessCodex is intentionally reserved (deferred — see issue #24).
	// Adding it = one registry entry + one TargetHarness value; no other change.
)

// SkillWriteMode selects how a rendered skill is committed to disk.
type SkillWriteMode int

const (
	// WriteMarkerMerge edits an existing on-disk SKILL.md, replacing only the
	// BEGIN/END marker region and preserving hand-authored prose. Claude Code only.
	WriteMarkerMerge SkillWriteMode = iota
	// WriteFullFile writes the rendered output as a fresh, fully-generated file
	// (no pre-existing file, no hand-authored prose to preserve). OpenCode.
	WriteFullFile
)

// AgentEmitter emits the per-role agent files for one harness (or is a no-op).
// The Codex slot and a future OpenCode-hooks emitter both satisfy this same
// interface, so adding them needs no change to the orchestrator.
type AgentEmitter interface {
	// Emit returns the agent files (path + content) for the given roles.
	// A no-op emitter returns (nil, nil).
	Emit(root string, roles map[protocol.RoleId]RoleSpec, figuresDir string, opts GenerateOptions) ([]GeneratedFile, error)
}

// ManifestEmitter emits a harness's distribution manifest (e.g. opencode.json).
// A no-op emitter returns (nil, nil). Same-shaped seam the future Codex
// `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` will reuse.
type ManifestEmitter interface {
	Emit(root string, opts GenerateOptions) ([]GeneratedFile, error)
}

// GeneratedFile is a (path, content) pair produced by an emitter, written by
// the orchestrator. Decoupling render from write lets every harness share one
// write/diff path.
type GeneratedFile struct {
	Path    string
	Content string
}

// TargetHarness carries everything that varies per harness.
type TargetHarness struct {
	Name HarnessName

	// SkillPath maps a canonical skill dir name to this harness's output path.
	//   claude-code -> <root>/skills/<dir>/SKILL.md
	//   opencode    -> <root>/.opencode/skill/<dir>/SKILL.md
	SkillPath func(root, dir string) string

	// SkillTemplate / SubSkillTemplate name the embedded template for role and
	// command skills. Claude Code uses the existing templates; OpenCode uses a
	// leaner template (drops the Claude-only `skills:` list — O-4).
	SkillTemplate    string
	SubSkillTemplate string

	// SkillWrite selects marker-merge (claude-code) vs full-file (opencode).
	SkillWrite SkillWriteMode

	// Agents emits per-role agent files for this harness (no-op for none).
	Agents AgentEmitter

	// Manifest emits the harness distribution manifest (UAT-D2). OpenCode emits
	// a minimal opencode.json; Claude Code is a no-op (its plugin.json stays
	// hand-maintained). nil == no-op.
	Manifest ManifestEmitter

	// Verbatim lists hand-authored skill dirs copied verbatim into this
	// harness's skill tree (protocol, install-cli). nil for claude-code (in place).
	Verbatim []string
}
```

Registry + flag wiring in `tools/codegen/main.go`:

```go
var harnessRegistry = map[codegen.HarnessName]codegen.TargetHarness{
	codegen.HarnessClaudeCode: codegen.ClaudeCodeTarget,
	codegen.HarnessOpenCode:   codegen.OpenCodeTarget,
}

// -targets=claude-code (default) reproduces today's output byte-for-byte
// (UAT-D1: only the target NAME changed, not the bytes).
targetsFlag := flag.String("targets", "claude-code",
	"comma-separated harness targets to emit: claude-code,opencode")
```

`ClaudeCodeTarget` (in `harness.go`) wraps the existing path/template/marker-merge behavior so the default `-targets=claude-code` run routes through the abstraction yet produces identical bytes; `Manifest` is nil (Claude plugin.json stays hand-maintained). `OpenCodeTarget` carries the OpenCode skill template, `.opencode/skill/<dir>/SKILL.md` path, `WriteFullFile`, the OpenCode agent emitter (S3), the `opencode.json` manifest emitter (S5), and `Verbatim: ["protocol","install-cli"]`.

A single orchestrator (`harness.go`) replaces the inline loops in `main.go`:

```go
func EmitHarness(h TargetHarness, root, figuresDir string,
	roleDirs map[protocol.RoleId]string, commandDirs map[string]string,
	opts GenerateOptions) ([]GeneratedFile, error)
```

It (1) renders + writes role skills, (2) renders + writes command skills, (3) copies `Verbatim` dirs, (4) calls `h.Agents.Emit`, (5) calls `h.Manifest.Emit` if non-nil. `ValidateGlobalIds()` stays harness-neutral and runs once after all harnesses.

**The only renderer change** (per the locked scope): thread a template name through the two renderers, defaulting to today's constant so existing call sites are untouched:

```go
// skills.go
const (
	TemplateSkill    = "templates/skill.go.tmpl"
	TemplateSubSkill = "templates/skill_sub.go.tmpl"
)
func renderSkill(roleId protocol.RoleId, figuresDir, tmplName string) (string, error)     // was (roleId, figuresDir)
func renderSubSkill(commandId, figuresDir, tmplName string) (string, error)               // was (commandId, figuresDir)
```

`renderAgent` is untouched (the OpenCode agent dialect is a *new* emitter + template, not a reparametrization of the Claude one).

