## 4. Slice decomposition (interface-first; R1 foundation first)

| Slice | Req | Deliverable | Owns (files) |
|-------|-----|-------------|--------------|
| **SLICE-1** | R1 | `TargetHarness` abstraction + registry + `-targets` flag (default `claude-code`) + renderer template-threading; `ClaudeCodeTarget` routes through it; **byte-identical default-output golden guard** | `internal/codegen/harness.go` (new), `internal/codegen/skills.go` (renderer params + template consts), `tools/codegen/main.go` (flag/loop/comment-fix), `internal/codegen/harness_test.go` + `testdata/harness.yaml` (new) |
| **SLICE-2** | R2 | OpenCode skill emission (29 skills) to `.opencode/skill/<dir>/SKILL.md` | `internal/codegen/templates/opencode_skill.go.tmpl` + `opencode_skill_sub.go.tmpl` (new), OpenCode skill path/writer wiring in `harness.go`, tests |
| **SLICE-3** | R3 | OpenCode agent emission to `.opencode/agent/<role>.md` (mode/model/permission) | `internal/codegen/opencode_agent.go` (new: emitter + 3 lookup tables), `internal/codegen/templates/opencode_agent.go.tmpl` (new), wire `OpenCodeTarget.Agents`, model-id + permission tests |
| **SLICE-4** | R5 | CopyVerbatim hand-authored skills (protocol, install-cli) into `.opencode/skill/` | `harness.go` (`copyVerbatimSkill` + `Verbatim` wiring), tests |
| **SLICE-5** | R4 | Minimal committed `opencode.json` ($schema + explicit `skills.paths`) | `internal/codegen/opencode_manifest.go` (new: `openCodeManifestEmitter` + `openCodeConfig`), wire `OpenCodeTarget.Manifest`, manifest tests |
| **SLICE-6** | R6/R7 | nix system-wide install: fix skills-path bug; add OpenCode agent + plugin global targets; optional global opencode.json | `nix/hm-module.nix`, nix eval check |

**Slicing principle:** SLICE-1 is the interface-first foundation — it lands the abstraction and *proves it preserves Claude Code output* before any OpenCode bytes exist. SLICE-2/3/5 are pure additive codegen behind the seam. SLICE-4/6 are file-placement + nix. Every slice is independently testable and reversible. The Codex slot and the `.mjs` hooks emitter both reuse `TargetHarness` + `AgentEmitter` + `ManifestEmitter` unchanged (future epics).

*(IMPL_PLAN note — c1 file-ownership: SLICE-1 OWNS the `harness.go` `TargetHarness`/`OpenCodeTarget` struct literal; SLICE-2/3/4/5 each ADD their field — `SkillPath`/`SkillWrite`, `Agents`, `Verbatim`, `Manifest` — to that shared literal, so the Phase-8 plan must give each slice its own new file and either serialize the one-line literal edits or have S1 pre-wire all field assignments to per-slice constructors to avoid parallel-worker collisions.)*

